steps.message:
The issue was that background styles were not preserved across terminal-wrapped lines when `soft_wrap=True` was used in `Console.print`. This happened because `rich` sent the entire styled segment as a single block, and many terminals do not automatically continue background colors on wrapped lines.

I fixed this by modifying `Console._render_buffer` to split segments that have a background color into chunks of `self.width` columns. Each chunk is rendered with its own style start and end codes, ensuring that the background color is reapplied at the start of each wrapped line.

